    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and all tests pass (the suite's only test class is `AcceptanceTest`; the other files are support classes).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived, read-only `ownerSegment` field to the Owner API following the existing Spring/MapStruct/OpenAPI conventions in this repo.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an `ownerSegment` property to the Owner schema (a `string` enum of `PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`), matching the style of the existing `contactPreference`/`ageBand` enums. This drives the generated `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum`.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added the `@Mapping(target = \"ownerSegment\", ...)` binding plus a `ownerSegment(Owner)` helper:\n- **TIER** = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel(owner) >= 3`, else `STANDARD` (reusing the existing `membershipLevel` derivation).\n- **AREA** = `METRO` when `locality(owner)` is `NSW`, `VIC`, or `QLD`, else `REGIONAL` (reusing the existing `locality` derivation).\n\nThe two are joined as `<TIER>_<AREA>`. This keeps the logic consistent with how sibling derived fields (`locality`, `timezone`, `membershipLevel`) are computed in the mapper.",
